CORE
main.c
--32
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
memset through a pointer with two struct targets must leave the other one
alone. The store to each possible target is guarded, and on the branch where
it is not taken the old value is framed back; for an object split into
members that old value was renamed as the bare whole-struct symbol, which
nothing assigns once the members are separate, so it was unconstrained and
the struct the memset did not reach came back with arbitrary members. Fails
on a binary without the fix; stock CBMC 5.95 passes.
